WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.954
A building maintenance app should alert a resident
when a repair appointment changes.

00:00:04.954 --> 00:00:10.723
The scheduling server knows the resident's account,
but that knowledge does not give it a reachable

00:00:10.723 --> 00:00:13.112
network endpoint on the resident's phone.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:18.707
The phone may change networks, sit behind address
translation or have its application suspended.

00:00:18.707 --> 00:00:25.034
Treating the phone as an ordinary public HTTP server
leaves those constraints unexplained, even if

00:00:25.034 --> 00:00:27.939
the notification payload is only a few bytes.

00:00:27.939 --> 00:00:34.007
Instead, the device or platform establishes an
outbound delivery path that the backend can use

00:00:34.007 --> 00:00:34.717
indirectly.

00:00:34.717 --> 00:00:39.365
Now consider the phone being offline when the
appointment changes twice.

00:00:39.407 --> 00:00:45.804
Decide whether to retain both changes, replace the
first with the latest state, or simply notify the

00:00:45.804 --> 00:00:46.763
app to refresh.

00:00:46.763 --> 00:00:51.945
This is a product-level delivery policy, not a
detail solved by opening a socket.

00:00:51.945 --> 00:00:58.342
Keep the authoritative appointment in durable
storage so that reconnecting clients can recover
their

00:00:58.342 --> 00:01:01.732
current state even when a notification never
arrives.

00:01:01.732 --> 00:01:05.019
A library app user signs in on a phone and a tablet.

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:11.341
Each installation registers for platform
notifications and sends its current provider-issued
routing

00:01:11.341 --> 00:01:13.554
token to the authenticated backend.

00:01:13.554 --> 00:01:17.284
The backend associates both installations with the
account.

00:01:17.284 --> 00:01:23.163
When a reserved book becomes ready, the notification
service resolves the account to eligible

00:01:23.163 --> 00:01:25.945
installations and submits delivery requests.

00:01:25.945 --> 00:01:32.384
The account identifies the person; the tokens
identify destinations through the platform's
delivery

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:33.035
mechanism.

00:01:33.035 --> 00:01:35.767
Now uninstall and reinstall the phone app.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:40.970
Its routing information may change, while the
person's account remains the same.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:46.564
Registration updates and invalid-token cleanup are
therefore part of normal operation.

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:52.874
Logging out also requires a policy that prevents the
next device user from receiving the previous

00:01:52.874 --> 00:01:54.760
user's private notifications.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:00.940
Provider acceptance only says a delivery request
entered that provider's process; it does not prove

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.062
the message was displayed or read.

00:02:03.062 --> 00:02:08.992
A notification can prompt a fresh authorized read of
the library record instead of carrying all

00:02:08.992 --> 00:02:10.552
sensitive details itself.
